# Generated Microsoft Office binaries (docs/office/) are produced from markdown
# sources by scripts/gen-office.sh — see docs/office/README.md. Mark them binary
# so git never attempts a text diff/merge or line-ending normalization on them.
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary

# Structural ontology graph artifacts (main#855/#856, #820 C×T2) are generated,
# sorted JSON that parallel branches regenerate independently — a textual 3-way
# merge spuriously conflicts on the sorted node/edge arrays even when the two
# sides touched different source files (the feedback_parallel_panels_shared_file
# hazard). Route them through the union merge-driver
# (.claude/lib/ontology_gen/merge_driver.py): it parses both sides + base, unions
# nodes by id and edges by (src,dst,type), and re-serializes canonically — so a
# merge result is byte-identical to a fresh regenerate.
#
# .gitattributes only NAMES the driver; the driver COMMAND must be registered in
# each clone's local git config (it cannot live here). Run once per clone:
#     make setup-ontology-merge-driver
# or manually:
#     git config merge.ontology-codegraph.name 'ontology code-graph union merge'
#     git config merge.ontology-codegraph.driver \
#       'python3 .claude/lib/ontology_gen/merge_driver.py %O %A %B %P'
ontology/structural/code-graph.json merge=ontology-codegraph
ontology/structural/cross-repo-graph.json merge=ontology-codegraph
